# Every file as committed, byte for byte, on every system: no line-ending
# conversion. Files are compared by their bytes (LICENSE's SHA-256, the
# example's fixture hashes, axe-core's), and two web-platform-tests data
# files hold CR on purpose. Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf, as
# GitHub's Windows runners set it) checks text files out with CRLF.
* -text
